# Python bytecode. A `.pyc` was committed here by a `git add -A` and rode a
# promotion to staging before anyone noticed: it is a build artifact, it is
# version- and platform-specific (this one was cpython-314), and a stale one
# shadows the source it was built from. Ignore the whole class rather than the
# one file that got caught.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Local editor / OS noise, same reasoning.
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch written by caller-drift.yml's watchdog step at runtime; never committed.
wd-body.md
body.md
